      "srList" : [{
          "sentence" : "In the Freundlich model (eq 1 ), Kf is a constant that indicates the relative adsorption capacity of the adsorbent and n is a constant that refers to the intensity of the adsorption. 26 1 In the Langmuir model (eq 2 ), Q e is the amount of solute adsorbed per unit weight of the adsorbent at equilibrium, Ce is the concentration at equilibrium, Q m is the maximum capacity of adsorption, and b is the constant related to the adsorption free energy. 26 2 The adjustment parameters of the models were calculated using the Rosenbrock Quasi-Newton optimization method, included in the STATISTICA software.",
